e outlook)","t":"Crop ratings 35% G/E, 37% P/VP (week of 2026-10-18; +2 pts G/E since the report), harvest 41% done. Ratings-implied crop now 12.89m bales (was 12.99m at the report). Texas D2\u2013D4 drought 48% of area (week of 2026-10-13; +12 pts since the previous report). Week ending 2026-10-08: US commitments 5.25m running bales = 43% of USDA's 12.3m target vs a 5-yr norm of 49% at this point \u2014 behind pace, risk of a cut. Brazil shipped 1.40m bales Aug\u2013Sep 2026 (9% of USDA's 16.0m vs a norm of 11%; last year 1.18m) \u2014 on pace."},{"h":"Positioning","t":"COT 2026-10-13: managed money net +65.7k (3-yr COT index 78) \u2014 not at an extreme. On-call 2026-10-09: net old-crop +38.1k contracts; commercials' old-crop long/short ratio at the 19th pct of 3 yrs \u2014 mills light on futures cover, fixing should add buying."},{"h":"Price outlook","t":"**Modestly bearish.** Supportive: Texas drought, Mill fixation. Weighing: US balance sheet, World ex-China stocks, US export sales. ICE front month 80.10\u00a2 on 2026-10-19 (+3.5% over the past month). Outlook uses the latest crop progress, export sales, COT and on-call data available through 2026-10-20. Watch the next crop progress and export sales releases to confirm or challenge USDA's numbers."}]},"Corn":{"my":"2026/27","unit":"Million Metric Tons","changes":[{"region":"World","unit":"Million Metric Tons","Production":{"now":1293.75,"prev":1290.95,"chg":2.8},"Domestic Use":{"now":1320.47,"prev":1320.23,"chg":0.24},"Exports":{"now":210.72,"prev":210.08,"chg":0.64},"Imports":{"now":203.38,"prev":203.11,"chg":0.27},"Ending Stocks":{"now":280.44,"prev":272.1,"chg":8.34},"S/U":{"now":0.21237892568555136,"prev":0.2061004521939359,"chg":0.006278473491615449}},{"region":"United States","unit":"Million Bushels","Production":{"now":16034.0,"prev":15800.0,"chg":234.0},"Domestic Use":{"now":13005.0,"prev":12905.0,"chg":100.0},"Exports":{"now":3300.0,"prev":3275.0,"chg":25.0},"Imports":{"now":25.0,"prev":25.0,"chg":0.0}